###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Table I is captioned 'RMSEs' while the running text calls the same numbers 'mean absolute errors'; they are encoded as RMSE, following the caption.
# - CACE-SOG and CACE-LES are new registry methods (a CACE short-range model with a different long-range term each). The DP-SR / DP-SOG models of Table II (parameter counts only) are not encoded.
# - Table III also lists CACE-SOG without the BSA initialisation (0.25 meV/atom, 10.46 meV/A); only the default model is encoded. In Table IV the columns CC-ACE, 4G-HDNNP, NequIP-LR, Polar-LR and CACE-LES are literature values and are not encoded.
# - Further applications (aqueous KF, the water liquid-vapour interface with revPBE0-D3 data, water/Pt(111) with PBE-D3 data of 48,041 structures) are reported with MD-derived properties or errors that were not captured; they are not encoded.
# - mu_max (angular truncation, 2 for the dimers) is not mapped to mlips:numAngularBasis; nu_max = 2 is encoded as mlips:bodyOrder following cheng2024. Settings of the NaCl-cluster fits were not captured. Loss, optimizer and software are not stated in the parts read.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
